{title: 205 - Gleams of the Golden Morning}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #205 • GLEAMS OF THE GOLDEN MOR • 15.15.18.16}
{lyricist: S. J. Graham}
{composer: S. J. Graham}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 205}
{meta: tune GLEAMS OF THE GOLDEN MOR}
{meta: meter 15.15.18.16}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Am]The golden morning is fast approaching; Jesus [C7/Bb]soon will [Dm/A]come
[Dm/A]To take His [Gm/Bb]faithful and happy [F/C]children [C7/Bb]To their promised [Dm/A]home.
[Dm/A]O, we see the [F/C]gleams of the golden morning Piercing through this [Gm/Bb]night of [Dm/A]gloom!
[Dm/A]O, we see [Gm/Bb]the gleams of the golden [F/C]morning [Gm/Bb]That will burst [Dm/A]the tomb.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[C7]O, we see the gleams of the golden morning
[C7]piercing thro' [Dm/A]this night of [Bb]gloom!
[Dm/A]O, see the [C]gleams of the golden [C7/Bb]morning
[Dm/A]that will [F/C]burst [Am]the tomb.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Am]The gospel summons will soon be [C7/Bb]carried
[Dm/A]to [Gm/Bb]the nations [C7/Bb]round;
[Dm/A]The Bridegroom [F/C]then will cease to [Gm/Bb]tarry
[Dm/A]and [Gm/Bb]the trumpet sound.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Am]Attended by all the shining [C7/Bb]angels,
[Dm/A]Down [Gm/Bb]the flaming [C7/Bb]sky
[Dm/A]the Judge [F/C]will come, and will take his [Gm/Bb]people
[Dm/A]where [Gm/Bb]they will [F/C]not [Gm/Bb]die.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Am]The lov'd of earth who have long been [C7/Bb]parted,
[Dm/A]Meet [Gm/Bb]in that [F/C]glad [C7/Bb]day;
[Dm/A]The tears [F/C]of those who are broken [Gm/Bb]hearted
[Dm/A]shall [Gm/Bb]be wiped [F/C]away.
{end_of_verse}
